Subject: [PATCH] compose: a named --user-data-dir keeps one identity

A launch that names --user-data-dir stores its seed in
<user-data-dir>/apostate/identity and reuses it on every later launch.
That directory holds the cookies and logins, and a site that sees one
account on different hardware each visit has a strong signal.
--fingerprint=<seed> still wins, and a launch without --user-data-dir
draws a fresh identity and stores nothing. The file holds one seed and a
newline, so it can be pasted back as --fingerprint, and a corrupt file
is replaced once.

--- a/base/apostate/compose.cc
+++ b/base/apostate/compose.cc
@@ -1663,7 +1663,30 @@ std::optional<std::string> ComposeProfileForCurrentProcess(
     return std::nullopt;
   }
 
-  const SeedResolution seed = ResolveSeed(command_line);
+  // Chrome's resolved directory when the caller knows it, the explicit switch
+  // otherwise. Hoisted above the seed because the layer below --fingerprint
+  // is bound to this directory, and unchanged in what it means: font
+  // provisioning still reads it on every launch, named directory or not.
+  const FilePath state_root =
+      user_data_dir.empty()
+          ? command_line.GetSwitchValuePath(kUserDataDirSwitch)
+          : user_data_dir;
+  const FilePath state_directory =
+      state_root.empty() ? FilePath()
+                         : state_root.AppendASCII(kStateDirectoryName);
+
+  // The identity binds only when the launch *named* a directory. The test is
+  // the switch and not the resolved path, because Chrome always resolves one:
+  // a resolved path is no evidence that anybody asked for a persistent
+  // profile, and binding on it would make a bare launch sticky, which is the
+  // one thing the launch contract promises it is not. What gets written to is
+  // still the resolved path, because that is the directory the cookies
+  // actually land in when the named one turned out to be invalid and Chrome
+  // fell back.
+  const bool named_a_directory =
+      !command_line.GetSwitchValuePath(kUserDataDirSwitch).empty();
+  const SeedResolution seed = ResolveSeed(
+      command_line, named_a_directory ? state_directory : FilePath());
 
   std::string rejection;
   FieldOverrides overrides;
